## SQ-FCK-03 | copper pot on a lit campfire cooks bone broth from bone + glow lichen
@group A
@commands Copper pot on a lit campfire; `/data merge block` slot 0 `minecraft:bone`, slot 1 `minecraft:glow_lichen`, container slot `minecraft:bowl`; wait 15 s
@pass bone broth x2 in the output (the recipe has 2 ingredients, under the pot's 4)
@fails owner's report stands: find which recipe check rejects it (`CopperPotBlockEntity.getMatchingRecipe`)
@from batches/r1113/c3_a1.qb
> setblock 1010 -60 1080 minecraft:campfire[lit=true]
> setblock 1010 -59 1080 miners_delight:copper_pot
> data merge block 1010 -59 1080 {Inventory:{Items:[{Slot:0b,id:"minecraft:bone",Count:1b},{Slot:1b,id:"minecraft:glow_lichen",Count:1b},{Slot:5b,id:"minecraft:bowl",Count:2b}]}}
> data get block 1010 -59 1080
sleep 20
> data get block 1010 -59 1080
expect farmersdelight:bone_broth
look the second data get shows bone broth in the meal or output slot (row says x2: one bone and one lichen make one cook; judge the count against the recipe yield). If the first data get shows the items under another key than Inventory.Items, the merge missed: BATCH-FAULT

